1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
That rattle for the first few
seconds after you start your car?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Don't ignore it.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
It's a quick, metallic sound
right at startup...

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,000
...then it goes away once
the engine warms up.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,500
That pattern can point to a
stretched timing chain...

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
...or worn guides not getting
oil pressure fast enough.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
It's more noticeable on cold
mornings...

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
...when the oil is thicker and
takes longer to build pressure.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
One clue is not a diagnosis...

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
...worth checking before
it gets louder.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look —
Nick's Tire and Auto, on Euclid Avenue.
